#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:3
msgid ""
"`yaml` is a definitive library for [YAML](https://yaml.org/), the human "
"friendly data serialization standard. This library:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:6
msgid "Supports both YAML 1.1 and YAML 1.2 and all common data schemas,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:7
msgid ""
"Passes all of the [yaml-test-suite](https://github.com/yaml/yaml-test-"
"suite) tests,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:8
msgid ""
"Can accept any string as input without throwing, parsing as much YAML out"
" of it as it can, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:9
msgid "Supports parsing, modifying, and writing YAML comments and blank lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:11
msgid ""
"The library is released under the ISC open source license, and the code "
"is [available on GitHub](https://github.com/eemeli/yaml/). It has no "
"external dependencies and runs on Node.js as well as modern browsers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:14
msgid ""
"For the purposes of versioning, any changes that break any of the "
"documented endpoints or APIs will be considered semver-major breaking "
"changes. Undocumented library internals may change between minor "
"versions, and previous APIs may be deprecated (but not removed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:17
msgid ""
"The minimum supported TypeScript version of the included typings is 3.9; "
"for use in earlier versions you may need to set `skipLibCheck: true` in "
"your config. This requirement may be updated between minor versions of "
"the library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:21
msgid ""
"For more information, see the project's documentation site: "
"[**eemeli.org/yaml**](https://eemeli.org/yaml/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:23
msgid ""
"For build instructions and contribution guidelines, see "
"[docs/CONTRIBUTING.md](docs/CONTRIBUTING.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:25
msgid "To install:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:27
msgid ""
"npm install yaml\n"
"# or\n"
"deno add jsr:@eemeli/yaml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:33
msgid ""
"**Note:** These docs are for `yaml@2`. For v1, see the [v1.10.0 "
"tag](https://github.com/eemeli/yaml/tree/v1.10.0) for the source and "
"[eemeli.org/yaml/v1](https://eemeli.org/yaml/v1/) for the documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:35
msgid "API Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:37
msgid ""
"The API provided by `yaml` has three layers, depending on how deep you "
"need to go: [Parse & Stringify](https://eemeli.org/yaml/#parse-amp-"
"stringify), [Documents](https://eemeli.org/yaml/#documents), and the "
"underlying [Lexer/Parser/Composer](https://eemeli.org/yaml/#parsing-"
"yaml). The first has the simplest API and \"just works\", the second gets"
" you all the bells and whistles supported by the library along with a "
"decent [AST](https://eemeli.org/yaml/#content-nodes), and the third lets "
"you get progressively closer to YAML source, if that's your thing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/yaml/README.md:40
msgid ""
"A [command-line tool](https://eemeli.org/yaml/#command-line-tool) is also"
" included."
msgstr ""

